# Everything installed here is machine-local and never committed: Coal, cuRobo and its source
# clone, each of them multi-gigabyte, licence-bound and specific to one machine. Only this file,
# the README and the lockfiles are tracked, so the folder and the install convention live in the
# repository while the payload stays out of git.
#
# locks/ is the exception on purpose: those files are input to the install, not output of it. They
# pin every conda package down to its URL and hash, which is what makes a rebuild reproducible and
# what keeps a rebuild off package builds that a Windows application-control policy refuses to
# load. README.md states that rule.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!locks/
!locks/*.lock
